<<<
function(
  firstArgument, secondArgument, third,
  fourth
);
>>> (trailing_commas=add_when_chopped) A chopped list gets a comma.
function(firstArgument, secondArgument, third);
<<<
function(
  firstArgument,
  secondArgument,
  third,
);
>>> (trailing_commas=add_when_chopped) A source comma still chops, and the chopped list keeps a comma.
foo(a, b,);
<<<
foo(
  a,
  b,
);
>>> (trailing_commas=add_when_chopped) Kept breaks grouping several items do not count as chopped.
